<script type="text/javascript">
    // Bisect AB at E; describe BF (= EL) on EB similar to D, and GH equal to
    // BF + C and similar to D (VI.25); make FLM = KH and FEN = KG, complete
    // MN, draw the diameter FO and describe the figure. The gnomon XWV is
    // MN less EL, so equals C; AO = AN + EO = LP + EO equals the gnomon.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the parallelograms only as the filled pieces FP
    // (EFMP) and AO, with FO, LQ, EN and the gnomon's arc XWV. The proof
    // builds the figure in an order those pieces cannot show, so AB, the
    // outline of BF, and the sides LM, MO, NO are solid slide twins over
    // Joyce's lines, hidden at rest (initiallyHidden), as on IV.13.
    //
    // Everything else added is transparent: EL's sides FL, FE, the segments
    // AE, EB, FLM, FEN, KH, KG, the parallelograms MN, AN, NB, LP, EO, QP,
    // AOt (a faceless twin of Joyce's filled AO, which would be raised over
    // EN and LQ when highlighted, #140), and the gnomon region XWVg (the
    // hexagon LMONEB; Joyce's XWV is the arc that marks it). The prose
    // reaches them as {AO|AOt}, {XWV|XWVg}, {VWX|XWVg}. A2 is the unlettered
    // corner of AO under A. No angle in the argument; no markers.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, D2, D3, K sliders and
